    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d490">

                <pb facs="0773" n="683" sameAs="frus:frus1932v02/pg683"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890G.01/330</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé in Great Britain (Atherton) to the British
                        Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs (Simon)</hi><anchor n="27" xml:id="d490-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 251</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-09-20">September 20, 1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to my note No.
                    219 of August 26 last<anchor n="28" xml:id="d490-f2"/> and to previous
                    correspondence regarding the release of Iraq from the mandatory régime, and in
                    compliance with instructions which I have received from my Government, to
                    enquire, in connection with the forthcoming vote on the admission of Iraq as a
                    member of the League of Nations, whether it is the intention of His Majesty’s
                    Government to lay before the appropriate body of the League the recent exchange
                    of correspondence regarding the right of the Government of the United States to
                    be consulted with respect to the conditions under which Iraq is to be
                    administered upon the termination of the mandated régime.</p>
                <p>In explanation of this enquiry I am desired to state that if His Majesty’s
                    Government does not intend to take the action indicated my Government will wish
                    to do so in view of the importance which it attaches to having its position in
                    the matter made clear to the members of the League.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ray
                                Atherton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d490-f1" n="27" type="source" xml:id="d490-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to the Department by the Chargé in his despatch No. 368 of the
                    same date; received September 30.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d490-f2" n="28" xml:id="d490-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed. This note merely expressed the Department’s appreciation for the
                    information supplied by the Foreign Office in its note of July 22.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
